"text": "Now the jets. These are cold-gas thrusters: a tank of compressed gas, some valves, and nozzles. No fuel. No flame. Push gas out one way, and the car gets pushed the other way, like letting go of a balloon. Fire a nozzle up on one side and down on the other, and the car rolls. Fire the opposite pair, and the roll stops. Tesla says it worked with SpaceX to make thrusters like these work in air, not just in space. Watch the launch again: the ramp provides the speed and the height, and the jets help manage the rotation and the landing. What none of this shows is sustained flight, a useful flying range, or anything certified to carry people through the air.",
